{{also|levant}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{bor|en|fr|levant||[[rising]], sun's point of rising}}, form of {{m|fr|lever||to rise}}, from {{der|en|la|levō||to rise}} (cf. also the present participle {{m|la|levans}}), from {{m|la|levis||light, not heavy}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ænt|lang=en}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# The countries bordering the eastern [[Mediterranean Sea]], namely [[Syria]], [[Lebanon]], [[Israel]], [[Palestine]], [[Jordan]] and [[Cyprus]] (and sometimes also including [[Turkey]] and [[Egypt]]).
# An [[easterly]] wind, generally in the western Mediterranean Sea

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|wind}} {{l|en|levanter}}

====Antonyms====
* {{l|en|Maghreb}} <!-- western Mediterranean, literally “where the sun sets” -->

